  "_answersComment": [
    "ebird-request-economy (decisions.md D-02), extended by ebird-store-hygiene.",
    "Whole checklist/view BODIES, not observations: each row is what eBird",
    "answered with HTTP 200, the `fields` flag the caller sent, and the verdict",
    "BOTH transports must reach for it: `status` 502 (a failed answer, so the",
    "escapee check writes no ledger entry and no stamp) or 200 with the number of",
    "species rows returned, and, where a row carries `first`, the first species",
    "row's breeding code and media.",
    "",
    "The body is sent as JSON when a row has `body`, as that text in UTF-8 when it",
    "has `text`, and as those exact bytes when it has `hex` (byte-level rows are",
    "hex so that no invisible character is ever written into this file).",
    "",
    "A body that is not JSON, or not a JSON object, is a FAILED answer in every",
    "mode. In the species-reading modes (no flag, and `provenance`) so is an",
    "observation list that is absent, null or anything but a JSON array, or an",
    "array holding an item that is not an object whose species code is absent,",
    "null or text. An empty array is still an answer. A breeding code or media",
    "count of the wrong shape reads as absent, never as a failure. Loaded by the",
    "same two parity suites as `cases` above, which drive the SHIPPED desktop",
    "service and the SHIPPED route."
  ],
